        "_kv_rules_tables": {
            "key": {
                "lookup_hardcoded": "armour_roll_lower_cap;;;;;the minimum percentage of armour roll that can be applied:::::armour_roll_max_value;;;;;this is the max valued that is allowed for the armour roll. If set to -1 there will be no maximum.:::::armour_roll_min_value;;;;;this is the min valued that is allowed for the armour roll. If set to -1 there will be no minimum.:::::attack_interval_multiplier_when_entity_attack_interrupted;;;;;How much times the cap to the interval between two subsequent melee or missile attacks gets multiplied in the event that the entity gets knocked back or knocked down.:::::battle_camera_max_distance_from_army;;;;;the maximum distance the camera can move from the player\'s army:::::battle_pipe_climb;;;;;Cost multiplier for moving through these pipe types (PT_WALL_CLIMB, PT_DESTROYED_WALL_CLIMB, PT_WOOD_WALL_CLIMB, PT_DESTROYED_WOOD_WALL_CLIMB, PT_CLIMB_LADDER):::::battle_pipe_default;;;;;Default cost multiplier for moving through pipes not specified explicitly in this table:::::battle_pipe_jump;;;;;Cost multiplier for moving through these pipe types (PT_JUMP, PT_JUMP_RAMP, PT_JUMP_ANIM):::::battle_pipe_jump_disembark;;;;;Cost multiplier for moving through this pipe type (PT_JUMP_DISEMBARK):::::battle_pipe_ship_grapple;;;;;Cost multiplier for moving through this pipe type (PT_SHIP_GRAPPLE):::::battle_pipe_siege_tower_wall_door;;;;;Cost multiplier for moving through this pipe type (PT_WALL_DOOR) when owned by siege tower:::::battle_pipe_wall_door;;;;;Cost multiplier for moving through this pipe type (PT_WALL_DOOR):::::battleai_sallyout_defend_settlement_preference;;;;;If ( defensive AI\'s non-tower CP / attacking army\'s total CP ) - ( (defensive AI\'s total CP - attacking army\'s ranged CP) / defensive AI\'s total CP ) is > this value, the AI will Sally Out because the attacker\'s missile strength is too great to withstand.:::::battleai_sallyout_open_field_victory_factor;;;;;If the defensive AI\'s army strength is this times greater than the attacking army strength, the AI will Sally Out of a settlement:::::battleai_sallyout_tower_strength;;;;;Approximate combat potential for a defensive tower, used by the AI to determine when to Sally Out of a settlement:::::battlefield_zone_slot_threshold;;;;;max distance in metres that can exist between two slots when occupying zones:::::bayonet_melee_attack_bonus;;;;;Using bayonets increases the attack stat of a unit:::::bayonet_ring_reload_time_penalty;;;;;Using Ring bayonets increases the time needed to reload the musket/carbine:::::berserk_inflicted_hitpoints_ratio;;;;;The amount of HP damage we have to do to trigger beserk. (Relative to our unit numbers):::::berserk_tick_timeout;;;;;The amount of battle ticks idle before berserk times out.:::::boiling_oil_distance_multiplier;;;;;Multiplied  distance from the front of the gate which will cause damage to units from oil:::::boiling_oil_flow_duration;;;;;Number of seconds the boiling oil flows for between intervals:::::braced_angle_for_collision_damage;;;;;half-angle, where an entity can be considered as braced to apply a braced mass multiplier to collision damage:::::bracing_attack_angle;;;;;half-angle, where a bracing entity will perform a bracing attack vs an incoming charger:::::bracing_calibration_ranks;;;;;Number of ranks at which full bracing multiplier is applied. Beyond this number, bracing multiplier will be clamped.:::::bracing_calibration_ranks_multiplier;;;;;The full bracing multiplier applied at calibration ranks. Multiplier decreases linearly to 1.0 at rank = 1.:::::bracing_charge_reflector_bonus;;;;;Additonal bracing bonus (multiplied to mass) for charge reflectors:::::bracing_immovable_by_small_entity_mass;;;;;The braced mass (i.e. after multiplying by bracing multiplier) beyond which an entity cannot be push around by small entities with soft collision.:::::bracing_max_multiplier_clamp;;;;;Global max clamp on bracing multiplier after all mulitplier are applied, e.g. from special abilities.:::::break_off_ignore_collision_time;;;;;A timer that disables collision for the specified time when an entity that is breaking off collides with an enemy entity.:::::break_off_speed_and_direction_checks;;;;;Enables speed and direction checks for entity breaking off. Enabling this makes breaking off more sticky.:::::charge_cool_down_time;;;;;time over which to fade out charge bonus after charge complete:::::climbing_ladder_speed_modifier;;;;;speed modifier for ladder climbing - fast speed:::::climbing_walls_speed_modifier;;;;;speed modifier for wall climbing - fast speed:::::collision_damage_armour_penetration_ratio;;;;;ratio of damage that ignores armour:::::collision_damage_default;;;;;collision damage dealt if no attacker is identified:::::collision_damage_immunity_timer;;;;;Collision damage immunity timer from the same attacker:::::collision_damage_maximum;;;;;collision damage cap:::::collision_damage_modifier;;;;;(collision_power^collision_damage_normaliser) * collision_damage_modifier:::::collision_damage_normaliser;;;;;(collision_power^collision_damage_normaliser) * collision_damage_modifier:::::collision_disable_delay_knocked_back_vs_enemies;;;;;Delay before disabling collision on an enemy entity in a knocked back interrupt animation:::::collision_disable_delay_knocked_back_vs_friends;;;;;Delay before disabling collision on a friendly entity in a knocked back interrupt animation:::::collision_disable_delay_knocked_down_vs_enemies;;;;;Delay before disabling collision on an enemy entity in a knocked down interrupt animation:::::collision_disable_delay_knocked_down_vs_friends;;;;;Delay before disabling collision on a friendly entity in a knocked down interrupt animation:::::collision_disable_delay_knocked_flying_vs_enemies;;;;;Delay before disabling collision on an enemy entity in a knocked flying interrupt animation:::::collision_disable_delay_knocked_flying_vs_friends;;;;;Delay before disabling collision on a friendly entity in a knocked flying interrupt animation:::::collision_enable_death_distance_to_obstacles_threshold;;;;;Distance to scan for obstacles to see if collision should be disabled. This is for entites bigger than the value set in collision_disable_death_max_entity_size.:::::collision_enable_death_fadeout_alpha;;;;;Fade out alpha to use when collision is disabled for entities bigger than the value set in collision_disable_death_max_entity_size:::::collision_enable_death_max_entity_size;;;;;Entities of this size or smaller always disable collision when dead. 0-VS 1-S 2-M 3-L 4-VL.:::::collision_restitution_coefficient;;;;;Coefficient of restitution for entity collision physics:::::collision_speed_delta_threshold_knocked_back;;;;;instantaneous speed delta to trigger a knocked back interrupt:::::collision_speed_delta_threshold_knocked_down;;;;;instantaneous speed delta to trigger a knocked down interrupt:::::collision_speed_delta_threshold_knocked_flying;;;;;instantaneous speed delta to trigger a knocked flying interrupt:::::collision_speed_delta_threshold_step_back;;;;;instantaneous speed delta to trigger a step back interrupt:::::default_num_placeable_obstacles;;;;;The default number of obstacles (toggleable buildings) can enable in battle:::::defense_line_pivot_factor;;;;;Sets how far down the pivot point is from the front of the formation. 0 = pivot from the front, 1 = pivot from the back:::::difficulty_mod_ai_easy_charge_bonus;;;;;:::::difficulty_mod_ai_easy_melee_attack;;;;;:::::difficulty_mod_ai_easy_melee_attack_interval;;;;;Multiplicative modifier to melee attack interval on easy for the AI only:::::difficulty_mod_ai_easy_melee_damage;;;;;:::::difficulty_mod_ai_easy_melee_defence;;;;;:::::difficulty_mod_ai_easy_missile_reload_additional;;;;;:::::difficulty_mod_ai_hard_charge_bonus;;;;;:::::difficulty_mod_ai_hard_melee_attack;;;;;:::::difficulty_mod_ai_hard_melee_attack_interval;;;;;Multiplicative modifier to melee attack interval on hard for the AI only:::::difficulty_mod_ai_hard_melee_damage;;;;;:::::difficulty_mod_ai_hard_melee_defence;;;;;:::::difficulty_mod_ai_hard_missile_reload_additional;;;;;:::::difficulty_mod_ai_very_hard_charge_bonus;;;;;:::::difficulty_mod_ai_very_hard_melee_attack;;;;;:::::difficulty_mod_ai_very_hard_melee_attack_interval;;;;;Multiplicative modifier to melee attack interval on very hard for the AI only:::::difficulty_mod_ai_very_hard_melee_damage;;;;;:::::difficulty_mod_ai_very_hard_melee_defence;;;;;:::::difficulty_mod_ai_very_hard_missile_reload_additional;;;;;:::::discard_defensive_feature_distance;;;;;If a hill is over this distance away, it will not be considered:::::entity_attack_interval_and_damage_modifier_vs_heroes;;;;;The mutliplier to use to modify the attack interval and damage done from a regular unit entity against a hero entity. So e.g. if this is 2.0, we double the attack interval and attack damage so the dps will remain the same but the entities will attack the hero less. (default 1.0 - no change):::::entity_formation_spacing;;;;;Separation in metres between the entity formation slots:::::entity_time_to_reach_optimum_tracking_threshold;;;;;Time (in seconds) before entity will track correctly after starting movement:::::escalation_level_one_building_health;;;;;Health of buildings for custom battle in escalation level 1:::::escalation_level_one_wall_breaches;;;;;:::::escalation_level_one_wall_health;;;;;:::::escalation_level_two_building_health;;;;;Health of buildings for custom battle in escalation level 2:::::escalation_level_two_wall_breaches;;;;;:::::escalation_level_two_wall_health;;;;;:::::fire_damage_only_applies_to_siege_equipment;;;;;Whether the fire damage applies only to siege equipment or to all entities (chariots, engines, etc.):::::fire_on_walls_accuracy_modifier;;;;;:::::fire_on_walls_reload_modifier;;;;;:::::fire_volley_arrow_min_threshold;;;;;:::::fire_volley_gun_min_threshold;;;;;:::::fire_volley_max_aim_delay_training_ratio;;;;;This increases (linearly) the initial delay to aiming, the poorer the training of the unit:::::firing_drill_improved_platoon_fire_reload_modifier;;;;;:::::firing_drill_mass_fire_reload_modifier;;;;;:::::firing_drill_platoon_fire_reload_modifier;;;;;:::::firing_drill_rank_fire_reload_modifier;;;;;:::::fort_wall_visibility_enabled;;;;;In fort battles, the walls give a perimeter visibility for the defender.:::::fort_wall_visibility_perimeter_distance;;;;;The distance the defender can see from unmanned fort walls.:::::free_for_all_last_man_standing_bonus_ratio;;;;;Ratio of players starting score/strenth that is awarded for being the last remaining player:::::general_auto_survive_threshold;;;;;When the percentage of alive entities in the general\'s unit is above this value the general cannot be killed.:::::hero_dismount_chance_vs_reflect_units;;;;;The chance of a hero being dismounted when charging against a charge reflector/negator:::::hero_duel_allowed_time_to_accept_reject;;;;;Time allowed to respond to a duel proposition from another player/ai. After this time has elapsed, a default option will be choosen (Accept).:::::hero_duel_blocking_allow_attack_when_max_missed_attacks_reached;;;;;0 - False 1 - True. If we allow a \"free\" attack when the missed attack limit is reached, this will ignore the block total but ensures the duel doesnt become stale with all blocks and no hits:::::hero_duel_blocking_decay_modifier;;;;;The amount to decay the block chance when performing a block in place of an attack. Once this chance reaches 0, an attack can be played without a responding block. Formula for calculating the decrease when blocking - hero_duel_blocking_decay_modifier * (attacker__m_damage / defender_m_damage):::::hero_duel_blocking_defence_modifier;;;;;This value multiplied by the entities melee defence with decide the starting blocking total. So if 10 and melee defence is 10 then the entity will have a max total of 100. Every attack the entity could hit with will change to a miss so the opponent will block, if this value is > 0. When this is the case, the value will decay:::::hero_duel_blocking_enabled;;;;;0 - False 1 - True. If we use the extra blocks system for duels:::::hero_duel_blocking_max_cached_attacks;;;;;The max number of attacks to cache when we play a block/miss instead of hit. The number of cached attacks will be multiplied by the damage done when a succesfull attack lands. -1 means no limit:::::hero_duel_blocking_recovery_modifier;;;;;Used to calculate the recovery per tick. Formula - (melee_defence / hero_duel_blocking_defence_modifier) * hero_duel_blocking_recovery_modifier. If the recovery value per tick resolves to be too high (greater than the decay rate), then the entity may never be allowed to land an attack:::::hero_duel_blocking_unmounted_vs_unmounted_only;;;;;0 - False 1 - True. If we use the extra blocks system for duels, only when both heroes are dismounted, else enabled for the mounted charge phase too:::::hero_duel_brawl_chance;;;;;Chance of a brawl after the hero_duel_time_between_brawls has elapsed (0-1):::::hero_duel_brawl_time_max;;;;;Max brawl time (seconds):::::hero_duel_brawl_time_min;;;;;Min brawl time (seconds):::::hero_duel_brawl_to_circle_chance;;;;;Chance of transitioning to a circle after a brawl (0-1):::::hero_duel_circle_radius;;;;;Radius of the circle phase.:::::hero_duel_circle_to_brawl_chance;;;;;Chance of transitioning to a brawl after a circle (default: 0.55):::::hero_duel_circle_turn_target_radians;;;;;The turn amount the hero will travel when in the circle state (in radians, 2pi default: 6.2831):::::hero_duel_dismount_chance_modifier;;;;;Modifier to apply when calculating the base dismount chance (default: 1) (BASE CHANCE: attacking_hero_exp / attacked_hero_exp * damage_proportion * THIS):::::hero_duel_dismount_target;;;;;Target at which the hero will be dismounted in a duel. This value will decay and each bit of damage done to the unit will sum towards this. Each successful strike done by this unit will replenish this target a bit  (default: 0.6):::::hero_duel_dismount_target_decay_per_second;;;;;The amount per second that the hero_duel_dismount_target will reduce by (default: 0.004):::::hero_duel_dismount_target_decay_recovery_per_hit;;;;;The amount that hero_duel_dismount_target will gain per successful strike (default: 0.008):::::hero_duel_man_vs_mount_bonus_dismount_chance_modifier;;;;;Bonus dismount chance modifier to apply to an un-mounted hero when facing a mounted hero. This is multiplied with the base chance calculated. (default: 5):::::hero_duel_reposition_distance;;;;;Distance to move after the charge phase (default: 17.5):::::hero_duel_sparing_killing_blow_damage_modifier;;;;;The amount of the percentage of remaining hp to remove when a killing blow is spared by the attacking hero in duel.:::::hero_duel_survival_time_calculation_constant;;;;;:::::hero_duel_survival_time_to_survive_seconds_max;;;;;The absolute maximum time to allow in duel survival goal:::::hero_duel_survival_time_to_survive_seconds_min;;;;;The absolute minimum time to allow in duel survival goal:::::hero_duel_time_before_dismount_allowed;;;;;The time (seconds) to elapse in a duel until a dismount chance is allowed. 0 == can dismount anytime:::::hero_duel_time_between_brawls;;;;;Min time between brawl phases (default: 30):::::hitpoint_threshold_to_fall_through_collision;;;;;Entities with this many hitpoints or less will fall through hard collision (e.g. over ledges, cliffs, etc):::::impact_reflection_attack_cooldown_timer;;;;;for pikes - time before the same defender can be attacked by the same pikeman:::::impact_reflection_final_damage_modifier;;;;;for pikes - multiplied to damage result from combat rules to determine final pike damage:::::impact_reflection_knockback_chance;;;;;for pikes - chance of triggering a knockback on hitting:::::impact_reflection_velocity_bonus_damage_modifier;;;;;for pikes - multiplied to bearing_relative_speed between defender and pikeman to determine pike damage bonus:::::interrupt_mass_ratio_clamp_hit_reaction;;;;;attacker/defender mass ratio where no hit reactions will be triggered by rules:::::interrupt_mass_ratio_clamp_knockback;;;;;attacker/defender mass ratio where no knock backs will be triggered by rules, or cascading:::::interrupt_mass_ratio_clamp_knockdown;;;;;attacker/defender mass ratio where no knock downs will be triggered by rules, or cascading:::::interrupt_mass_ratio_clamp_melee_block;;;;;attacker/defender mass ratio where no melee blocks will be triggered by rules:::::interrupt_mass_ratio_clamp_stepback;;;;;attacker/defender mass ratio where no step backs will be triggered by rules, or cascading:::::jump_attack_chance;;;;;chance to trigger a jumping attack instead of a moving attack:::::jump_attack_chance_for_small_groups;;;;;chance to trigger a jumping attack instead of a moving attack for small groups / units / heroes:::::jump_attack_chance_vs_charge_reflection;;;;;chance to trigger a jumping attack instead of a moving attack against a unit having charge reflection:::::jump_attack_chance_vs_routing_target;;;;;chance to trigger a jumping attack instead of a moving attack against a routing unit (applied for small groups / units / heroes as well):::::knockdown_getting_up_delay_armour_multiplier;;;;;multiplied to the armour stat and then added to the randomised delay time generated from the randomiser:::::knockdown_getting_up_delay_max;;;;;maximum delay time for randomiser:::::knockdown_getting_up_delay_min;;;;;minimum delay time for randomiser:::::matched_combat_hero_vs_hero_cavalry_percentage;;;;;Percentage chance of using matched combat instead of async attacks for melee combat, for hero_vs_hero when at least one of them is cavalry.:::::matched_combat_hero_vs_hero_infantry_percentage;;;;;Percentage chance of using matched combat instead of async attacks for melee combat, for hero_vs_hero when both are infantry.:::::matched_combat_hero_vs_unit_percentage;;;;;Percentage chance of using matched combat instead of async attacks for melee combat, for hero_vs_units.:::::matched_combat_min_hitpoints_to_initiate;;;;;Percentage hit points remaining required to initiate matched combat.:::::matched_combat_min_hitpoints_whilst_active;;;;;When taking damage from sources not in the same combat witness, remaining hit points is clamped to this value to prevent entity from dying and prematurely terminating matched combat.:::::matched_combat_percentage;;;;;Percentage chance of using matched combat instead of async attacks for melee combat:::::matched_combat_unit_vs_hero_percentage;;;;;Percentage chance of using matched combat instead of async attacks for melee combat, for units_vs_heroes.:::::maximum_bastion_artillery_per_settlement;;;;;The maximum number of bastion artillery pieces the defender can have in a siege. Each settlement must have at LEAST this many slots, it can have more.:::::melee_attack_interval;;;;;delay after weapon hit before the next attack animation can start:::::melee_attack_threshold_modifier_artillery;;;;;Modifier applied to the number of entities in a unit to calculate how many entities have to be in combat to react, for artillery units:::::melee_attack_threshold_modifier_guard_mode_active;;;;;Modifier applied to the number of entities in a unit to calculate how many entities have to be in combat to react, when the unit is in guard mode:::::melee_attack_threshold_modifier_idle_ammo_remaining;;;;;Modifier applied to the number of entities in a unit to calculate how many entities have to be in combat to react, when the unit is idle AND has ammo AND unit missile weapon is not precursor AND unit has fire at will:::::melee_attack_threshold_modifier_idle_default;;;;;Modifier applied to the number of entities in a unit to calculate how many entities have to be in combat to react, default modifier:::::melee_attack_threshold_modifier_ordered;;;;;Modifier applied to the number of entities in a unit to calculate how many entities have to be in combat to react, when the unit is not idle:::::melee_defence_direction_penalty_coefficient_flank;;;;;coefficient by which defender\'s melee defence stat is multiplied by when attacked in the flank:::::melee_defence_direction_penalty_coefficient_rear;;;;;coefficient by which defender\'s melee defence stat is multiplied by when attacked in the rear:::::melee_defence_formed_attack_bonus;;;;;Added to base defend stat if defender is in formed attack.:::::melee_height_damage_modifier_max_coefficient;;;;;used in melee height damage modifier calculation:::::melee_height_damage_modifier_max_difference;;;;;used in melee height damage modifier calculation:::::melee_hit_chance_base;;;;;base melee hit chance, used in attack hit determination:::::melee_hit_chance_max;;;;;max melee hit chance, used in attack hit determination:::::melee_hit_chance_min;;;;;min melee hit chance, used in attack hit determination:::::melee_hit_chance_normalisation_coefficient;;;;;coefficient by which hit chance determination calculation is normalised:::::melee_mage_switch_to_melee_time;;;;;A hybrid melee-mage will casts spells unit the mana pool is this many seconds away from filling up to max (at base mana recharge rate.) After this point it will favor melee attack, until mana is no long so low.:::::melee_max_hit_reactions;;;;;Maximum number of hit reaction interrupts before entity ignores hit reactions to allow it the opportunity to attack (for regulars):::::melee_max_hit_reactions_for_hero_vs_hero;;;;;Maximum number of hit reaction interrupts before entity ignores hit reactions to allow it the opportunity to attack (for hero vs hero):::::melee_max_hit_reactions_for_heroes;;;;;Maximum number of hit reaction interrupts before entity ignores hit reactions to allow it the opportunity to attack (for heroes):::::melee_on_damage_effect_knock_chance_attacker_charging_bonus;;;;;Multiplied to base knock probabilities and charging factor to get bonus to add to knock chance when attacker is charging:::::melee_on_damage_effect_knock_chance_defender_charging_factor;;;;;Multiplier to knock chance when defender is charging:::::melee_on_damage_effect_knockback_chance;;;;;Multiplied to mass ratio (attacker/defender) to get base knockback probability on a melee hit:::::melee_on_damage_effect_knockdown_chance;;;;;Multiplied to mass ratio (attacker/defender) to get base knockdown probability on a melee hit:::::melee_outnumbered_defence_penalty;;;;;penalty multiplier applied to melee defence of entity who is attacked by multiple attackers:::::melee_secondary_attack_probability;;;;;the probability in range [0, 1] that a secondary melee attacker will be awarded an attack:::::melee_weapon_building_damage_mult;;;;;This multiplier is applied to the primary melee weapon damage when attacking buildings.:::::minimum_melee_attack_interval;;;;;The minimum possible melee attack interval in seconds. Dictates the fastest speed at which entities can fight. Needed because stat can max out, leading to a time of 0s:::::missile_accuracy_for_towers;;;;;Accuracy to use for arrow/cannon towers, when there are no entity stats.:::::missile_armour_penetrating_coefficient;;;;;multiplied by armour value during missile damage resolution:::::missile_armour_piercing_coefficient;;;;;multiplied by armour value during missile damage resolution:::::missile_height_damage_modifier_max_coefficient;;;;;used in missile height damage calculations:::::missile_height_damage_modifier_max_difference;;;;;used in missile height damage calculations:::::missile_ignore_own_unit_for_friendly_fire;;;;;Entities in own unit will be excluded from clear shot test and projectile collisions.:::::missile_lethality_coefficient_effective_range;;;;;used to determine letthality of projectile due to range, when target is within effective range:::::missile_lethality_coefficient_extreme_range;;;;;used to determine letthality of projectile due to range, once the projectile exceeds effective range:::::missile_saving_bonus_base;;;;;basic saving bonus to which shields and armour bonuses are added:::::missile_saving_bonus_coefficient;;;;;the sum of the armour and shield bonuses are multiplied by this value.:::::missile_shield_piercing_coefficient;;;;;multiplied by shield value during missile damage resolution:::::missile_target_in_cover_penalty;;;;;subtracted from hit chance in range [0, 1] when determine missile\'s accuracy against target in cover:::::move_backwards_minimum_distance;;;;;Minimum value the move backwards extent can be reduced to:::::move_backwards_minimum_distance_melee;;;;;Minimum value the move backwards extent during melee can be reduced to:::::move_backwards_radius_melee_modifier_default;;;;;Maximum seconds the entity can_move backwards from melee - used with walk speed to create radius of valid movement area:::::move_backwards_radius_modifier_default;;;;;Maximum seconds the entity can_move backwards for - used with walk speed to create radius of valid movement area:::::move_backwards_speed_percentage_default;;;;;Move backwards at this percentage of their walk_speed:::::move_backwards_vector_degrees_default;;;;;The degrees creating the move backwards valid movement area:::::night_battle_attacker_visibility_spotting_range_modifier;;;;;Unit record max visibility spotting range for attacking units in a night battle. Result will be THIS * m_visibility_spotting_range:::::night_battle_defender_visibility_spotting_range_modifier;;;;;Unit record max visibility spotting range for attacking units in a night battle. Result will be THIS * m_visibility_spotting_range:::::pike_attack_zone_cosine_angle;;;;;Pike attack cone in front of entity, in cosine(angle), e.g. cos(60) = 0.5:::::pike_attack_zone_depth;;;;;Pike attack cone depth (m):::::pike_lower_bearing_tolerance;;;;;Bearing delta from movement direction to lower or raise pikes (radians):::::pike_lower_delay_combat;;;;;Once locked in combat animation, this timer is set. Timer must run out before entity can lower pike.:::::pike_lower_delay_turn_rate_multiplier;;;;;Timer is set as long as entity bearing is not within pike_lower_bearing_tolerance. Timer must run out before entity can lower pike. This is a value multiplied to (Pi/turn rate), i.e. the time to do an about turn.:::::projectile_aiming_target_size_modifier;;;;;Introduce a random aim point error based on the radius or height of the target multiplied by this number.:::::projectile_arrow_deflect_chance_heroes;;;;;Specifies the chance of the damaging arrow being deflected onto the ground for hero entities (otherwise it will be visually stuck on the entity). It will always stick on dead heroes:::::projectile_arrow_deflect_chance_units;;;;;Specifies the chance of the damaging arrow being deflected onto the ground for regular entities (otherwise it will be visually stuck on the entity). It will always stick on dead entities:::::projectile_building_vs_single_entity_general_calibration_area_mod;;;;;Used to modify the target area for tower projectiles when against a single entity general unit:::::projectile_friendly_fire_man_height_coefficient;;;;;Friendly entities are enlarged by this co-efficient to make them fatter and harder to fire past. Be wary with reducing this. It was added to deal with exploit where players would put melee \'shield\' units in front of their missile units and fire through them (Original value: 1.3):::::projectile_friendly_fire_man_radius_coefficient;;;;;Friendly entities are enlarged by this co-efficient to make them fatter and harder to fire past. Be wary with reducing this. It was added to deal with exploit where players would put melee \'shield\' units in front of their missile units and fire through them (Original value: 2.2):::::projectile_unit_vs_single_entity_general_calibration_area_mod;;;;;Used to modify the target area for projectiles when against a single entity general unit:::::pursuit_charge_bonus_modifier;;;;;All attacks from pursuers against routers are treated as charges (get the charge bonus * pursuit_charge_bonus_modifier ):::::reform_distance_threshold_radius_fraction;;;;;This value multiplied by the entity radius is the distance threshold used for reforms:::::refusal_chance_vs_charge_negation;;;;;Cavalry refusal chance vs units with charge negation:::::refusal_chance_vs_heroes;;;;;Cavalry refusal chance vs heroes:::::refusal_chance_vs_pike_phalanx;;;;;Cavalry refusal chance vs pike phalanx:::::rules_charge_reflections_mass_ratio_override;;;;;For charge reflections, this value will be used as the mass ratio:::::rules_charge_reflections_mass_ratio_override_single_entity_heroes;;;;;For charge reflections involving single entity heroes as the charger, this value will be used as the mass ratio:::::scaled_playable_area_size_max;;;;;Playable area size scaled between min and max based on number of units:::::scaled_playable_area_size_min;;;;;Playable area size scaled between min and max based on number of units:::::settlement_destruction_max_melee_attack_penalty;;;;;Penalty which grows from zero to max as the settlement is destroyed:::::settlement_destruction_max_melee_defence_penalty;;;;;Penalty which grows from zero to max as the settlement is destroyed:::::shield_defence_angle_melee;;;;;Shield defense half-angle vs melee (deg):::::shield_defence_angle_missile;;;;;Shield defense half-angle vs missile (deg):::::shield_defence_angle_missile_turtle;;;;;Shield defense half-angle vs missile (deg), 180 is protected from all angles:::::shockwave_speed_delta_threshold_knocked_back;;;;;instantaneous speed delta to trigger a knocked back interrupt:::::shockwave_speed_delta_threshold_knocked_down;;;;;instantaneous speed delta to trigger a knocked down interrupt:::::shockwave_speed_delta_threshold_knocked_flying;;;;;instantaneous speed delta to trigger a knocked flying interrupt:::::shockwave_speed_delta_threshold_step_back;;;;;instantaneous speed delta to trigger a step back interrupt:::::spotting_distance_default;;;;;default distance at which units can spot other units:::::spotting_distance_hidden_reduction;;;;;spotting distance reduced when unit is hidden:::::store_hp_for_whole_composed_entity_group;;;;;If the value is 0 the HP will be stored at the composed entity group level (as defined in the land_units_templates table) otherwise they will be stored at the composed entity level.:::::tickets_multiple_victory_points;;;;;Sets the number of tickets to be used in a battle with multiple capture points, i.e. medium. large and extra large cities:::::tickets_single_victory_point;;;;;Sets the number of tickets to be used in a battle with a single capture point, i.e. small city, encampment, baggage train:::::unit_decay_scaling_ending_row;;;;;The units rank depth at which we start to scale the decay modifier (Used for staggering unit movement). Will be used with unit_decay_scaling_starting_row to scale the decay value for the units max rows. Should be > unit_decay_scaling_starting_row:::::unit_decay_scaling_starting_row;;;;;The units rank depth at which we start to scale the decay modifier (Used for staggering unit movement). Ranks below this will use the raw decay value, above this will use a percentage of this, calculated with  unit_decay_scaling_ending_row. Should be < unit_decay_scaling_ending_row:::::unit_firing_line_of_sight_considered_obstructed_ratio;;;;;When this ratio of the unit cannot see to fire, the unit\'s LOS is considered blocked:::::unit_max_drag_out_rank_depth_modifier;;;;;The value to be multiplied with the default unit rank depth to calculate the max drag width. Should be > 0:::::unit_max_drag_width;;;;;Maximum width in metres a unit can drag out to:::::unit_min_drag_out_rank_depth_modifier;;;;;The value to be multiplied with the default unit rank depth to calculate the min drag width. The result will scale with the entities remaining in the unit. Should be > 0:::::unit_spawn_offset;;;;;distance between unit spawn position and the ordered position:::::unit_threat_considered_even_fraction;;;;;Given the difference in cp deltas between 2 units, anything +/- this fraction will be considered an even matchup. E.g. UnitA:100 UnitB:105 Ratio:0.952 -> if ratio is greater than 1 - unit_threat_considered_even_fraction and less than 1 + unit_threat_considered_even_fraction then its even:::::unruly_enemy_range;;;;;The range to detect enemies to contribute to unruly taunt.:::::unruly_max_taunting_enemies;;;;;The max number of enemies in range to allow the taunt meter to fill. If more than this then the unit will \'decide\' it should not attack due to high loss probability.:::::unruly_min_health_remaining_ratio;;;;;The percentage health that must remain before a unit will consider going unruly (0.0 - 1.0).:::::unruly_taunt_level_increment;;;;;The number of taunt points per battle tick per enemy in range to gain/lose.:::::unruly_taunt_points_to_trigger;;;;;The number of taunt points needed to go unruly. Taunt points are accumlated every battle tick.:::::unruly_taunt_points_to_trigger_max;;;;;The max number of taunt points to accumulate.:::::unruly_timeout;;;;;After this period of time a unit will come to its senses and become controllable again, even if still in battle. (battle tick):::::unspottable_unit_reveal_distance;;;;;Range at which hidden unspottable units are revealed:::::ward_save_max_value;;;;;The maximum damage modification available:::::ward_save_min_value;;;;;The minimum damage modification available",
            },
        },
        "_kv_ui_tweakers_tables": {
            "key": {
                "lookup_hardcoded": "battle_camera_depth_of_field_bokeh_hotspot_kernel_size;;;;;(IN GAME) Depth of Field - Brightness kernel size of detecting hotspots for splat:::::battle_camera_depth_of_field_bokeh_intensity;;;;;(IN GAME) Depth of Field - Bokeh sprite splat intensity:::::battle_camera_depth_of_field_bokeh_sprite_radius;;;;;(IN GAME) Depth of Field - Radius of sprite used to splat bokeh:::::battle_camera_depth_of_field_bokeh_threshold;;;;;(IN GAME) Depth of Field - Brightness difference threshold for displaying bokeh:::::battle_camera_depth_of_field_focal_cross_size;;;;;(IN GAME) Depth of field - Width in pixels of the crosses used to focus the camera:::::battle_camera_depth_of_field_focal_depth_moving_average_weight;;;;;(IN GAME) Depth of field - The weight applied to the focal parameters from this frame - used to smooth transition during camera movement:::::battle_camera_depth_of_field_focal_far_falloff;;;;;(IN GAME) Depth of field - The fall off of focus in the background:::::battle_camera_depth_of_field_focal_near_falloff;;;;;(IN GAME) Depth of field - The fall off of focus in the foreground:::::battle_camera_depth_of_field_focal_ring_count;;;;;(IN GAME) Depth of field - The number of focal cross in the ring used to focus the camera:::::battle_camera_depth_of_field_focal_ring_radius;;;;;(IN GAME) Depth of field - Radius of the ring of crosses used to focus:::::battle_camera_depth_of_field_focal_target_height;;;;;(IN GAME) Depth of field - Focal target height on the screen as a proportion of the vertical resolution:::::battle_camera_depth_of_field_focal_width_dilation;;;;;(IN GAME) Depth of field - Dilation of the ring of focus:::::battle_camera_depth_of_field_heightmap_raycast_area_size;;;;;(IN GAME) Distance for additional raycase points(left, right, top and bottom) pints are placed around main(center) point.:::::battle_camera_depth_of_field_heightmap_raycast_height_threshold;;;;;(IN GAME) Campaign camera height limit to do fake raycast agains camera heightmap in order to detect focal depth more accurately.:::::battle_camera_depth_of_field_heightmap_raycast_steps;;;;;(IN GAME) Number of sections path between camera position and initial target is divided into when fake raycast is done for depth of field effect.:::::battle_camera_depth_of_field_kernel_radius_background;;;;;(IN GAME) Depth of Field - Radius of blur kernal in the background:::::battle_camera_depth_of_field_kernel_radius_foreground;;;;;(IN GAME) Depth of Field - Radius of blur kernal in the foreground:::::battle_camera_depth_of_field_kernel_radius_foreground_coc;;;;;(IN GAME) Depth of Field - Radius of blur kernal used to smudge the circle of confusion in the foreground:::::battle_capture_point_fade_end;;;;;start point in metres when capture point icons end fading (go invisible):::::battle_capture_point_fade_min;;;;;min opacity of capture point icons:::::battle_capture_point_fade_start;;;;;start point in metres when capture point icons start fading:::::battle_capture_point_spline_wall_height;;;;;Capture point splines in warhammer for garrisoned walls need to render on top of walls, this is the wall height for spline since wall not linked to capture point in anyway:::::battle_dragout_cat_icon_min_size;;;;;In new dragout outline system, min size for unit cat indicator (value used by indicator rendering system):::::battle_dragout_corner_length;;;;;In new dragout outline system, length of corner elements on back of outlines for units with more than one entity:::::battle_dragout_corner_length_single_entities;;;;;In new dragout outline system, length of corner elements for units with single entity (like generals):::::battle_dragout_height_off_ground;;;;;In new dragout outline system, height of new outline dragout system off of ground:::::battle_dragout_indicator_scale;;;;;In new dragout outline system, size of unit cat icons for units with more than one entity:::::battle_dragout_indicator_scale_single_entities;;;;;In new dragout outline system, size of unit cat icons for units with single entity (like generals):::::battle_dragout_rank_icon_height;;;;;In new dragout outline system, height of rank icons down side of outline:::::battle_dragout_rank_icon_width;;;;;In new dragout outline system, width of rank icons down side of outline:::::battle_dragout_spline_width;;;;;In new dragout outline system, width of splines for units with more than one entity:::::battle_dragout_spline_width_single_entities;;;;;In new dragout outline system, width of splines for units with single entity (like generals):::::battle_id_base_size;;;;;Banners base scale:::::battle_id_bob_height;;;;;How high banners move up when bobbing when selected:::::battle_id_bob_speed;;;;;How quickly banners bob when selected:::::battle_id_fade_duration_ms;;;;;Duration in ms for banner fade anim when too close:::::battle_id_fade_end;;;;;Metres camera from banner when fully faded out (not used for warhammer, code commented out):::::battle_id_fade_start;;;;;Metres camera from banner before fades out:::::battle_id_forest_height_offset;;;;;Banners extra height when unit in forested area, if want to raise above trees:::::battle_id_height;;;;;Banners height above entity:::::battle_id_highlight_unary_mouseover;;;;;0-1 value that specifies how much to brighten banner on mouseover:::::battle_id_highlight_unary_selected;;;;;0-1 value that specifies how much to brighten banner on selection:::::battle_id_max_size;;;;;Banners maximum scale based on distance:::::battle_id_scale_weight;;;;;How quickly banners scale based on distance:::::battle_leaf_clip_proximity;;;;;This is distance from the camera at which tree leaves will be clipped when leaf clipping option is enabled.:::::battle_leaf_clip_proximity_transition_off_time;;;;;the time it takes to turn off battle leaf proximity:::::battle_leaf_clip_proximity_transition_on_time;;;;;determines how time over which the battle leaf proximity clip happens - a smaller number results in a fast time clip to the full distance:::::battle_leaf_clip_strength;;;;;Strength of the culling of the leaves (falloff).  A larger value results in a greater falloff.:::::battle_multiple_selection_movement_long_mouse_down_time;;;;;Time (in seconds) the right mouse button must be held down to make a multiple selection maintain its formation:::::battle_unit_outline_opacity;;;;;Opacity of unit outlines rendered in battle when units behind geometry:::::campaign_agent_id_height;;;;;Height of agent ids:::::campaign_army_id_height;;;;;the height at which army IDs sit above the ground:::::campaign_army_strength_cp_force_min;;;;;Used for army relative strength calculation added in 3k.  This is the minimum cp value of a force.:::::campaign_army_strength_cp_general_max;;;;;Used for army relative strength calculation added in 3k.  This is the maximum cp value a general in records mode will have.:::::campaign_army_strength_cp_hero_max;;;;;Used for army relative strength calculation added in 3k.  This is the maximum cp value a unit will have.:::::campaign_army_strength_cp_unit_max;;;;;Used for army relative strength calculation added in 3k.  This is the maximum cp value a unit will have.:::::campaign_battle_site_marker_height;;;;;Height of battle site marker icons in campaign for indicating where can raise the dead:::::campaign_camera_zoom_height;;;;;How high the camera is from the target when zooming to things like settlements/characters:::::campaign_camera_zoom_offset;;;;;How far away the camera is from the target when zooming to things like settlements/characters:::::campaign_child_emperor_adulthood_year;;;;;the year where the child emperor will become an adult:::::campaign_citybar_camera_zoom_offset;;;;;Citybars can cover small settlements, this is an offset to compensate for that:::::campaign_citybar_distance_depth_render_boundary;;;;;Used to disable depth rendering when the distance is under the boundary:::::campaign_citybar_distance_toggle;;;;;When the citybar will toggle to another layout, distance from camera:::::campaign_citybar_height;;;;;Determines city info bars height over city:::::campaign_citybar_height_depth_render_boundary;;;;;If the camera gets above this height from the terrain, it stops depth rendering:::::campaign_citybar_height_offset;;;;;The height offset of the citybar (i.e. how far from the floor):::::campaign_citybar_offset_multiplier;;;;;Sets the offset of the city bar from the centre of the settlement (deprecated for database entry):::::campaign_flag_fade_duration_ms;;;;;How long in ms flag takes to fade out/in in campaign:::::campaign_flag_fade_start;;;;;How close can get to flags in campaign before fade out:::::campaign_flag_scale_end_distance;;;;;Distance to camera that scaling down of campaign flag will stop:::::campaign_flag_scale_min;;;;;Min amount will scale flag based on distance to camera:::::campaign_flag_scale_start_distance;;;;;Distance to camera that when reached will start scaling down campaign flags to not block camera:::::campaign_flag_settlement_height;;;;;This is height offset of campaign flags when over settlements for garrisoned characters:::::campaign_floating_ui_fade_end;;;;;Distance from floating ui when fully faded out:::::campaign_floating_ui_fade_start;;;;;Distance from floating ui when starts to fade:::::campaign_floating_ui_mid_fade_end;;;;;Distance from floating ui  (mid_height) when fully faded out:::::campaign_floating_ui_mid_fade_start;;;;;Distance from floating ui (mid_height) when starts to fade:::::campaign_floating_ui_supply_bar_max;;;;;The theoretical max of the supply system in 3k (and future games?) so we can resize bars accordingly:::::campaign_map_pin_height;;;;;(IN GAME) The default height of user/tutorial map pins in the campaign:::::campaign_pre_battle_even_force_strength_max_percentage;;;;;sets the maximum percentage of relative combat strength that will make the UI display that we have an even force strength:::::campaign_pre_battle_even_force_strength_min_percentage;;;;;sets the minimum percentage of relative combat strength that will make the UI display that we have an even force strength:::::campaign_tooltip_delay_ms;;;;;How long cursor has to be still until campaign tooltip appears:::::custom_battle_deployables_per_unit;;;;;The number of deployables each unit will raise the cap by:::::custom_battle_mountable_artillery_percent;;;;;Determines how many mountable artillery defender of siege gets based on this percentage of number of units in army (capped at 5 though):::::custom_battle_siege_equipment_percent;;;;;Percentage of units in army (that can use siege vehicles) that get a siege vehicle in custom battle:::::help_hint_delay_s;;;;;How many seconds before start highlighting help button under assumption player needs help in campaign (when they havent clicked/pressed anything for this duration):::::missile_damage_over_this_much_time;;;;;how much time do we want to display missile damage over i.e. 1.0 is DPS, 60.0 is damage per 60 seconds...per entity:::::tacmap_dbl_click_threshold_ms;;;;;determines time in ms as what counts as double press of shortcut for tactical toggle. If 0 will always toggle.:::::tacmap_face_current_direction;;;;;if true, camera direction will be in direction battle camera was in. Otherwise always faces \'north\' so like radar:::::tacmap_hold_threshold_ms;;;;;Only relevant if tacmap_dbl_click_threshold_ms != 0. determines time in ms as what counts as holding down tactical toggle (to avoid flicker when double tapping):::::tacmap_instant_transition;;;;;if true, no camera pans, just instant:::::tacmap_is_moveable;;;;;if true, allows to control camera movement with wasd/mouse scroll:::::tacmap_light_change_duration_ms;;;;;how long takes for lighting setting to change (fog to clear):::::tacmap_max_height;;;;;used to define max height can zoom out (lower if want to clamp max height can zoom out so cant see whole battlefield):::::tacmap_max_height_offset;;;;;extra height added onto height calculated can see whole battlefield:::::tacmap_min_height;;;;;how much can zoom in when moveable, value is distance from highest point on map can zoom into:::::tacmap_move_speed_multiplier;;;;;how quick moves with wasd/drag in tac map:::::tacmap_near_clip_height_threshold;;;;;If the tacmap camera height is greater than this, then tacmap_near_clip_max is used for near clip distance:::::tacmap_near_clip_max;;;;;Near clip distance used for tacmap camera wheight height is above tacmap_near_clip_height_threshold:::::tacmap_near_clip_min;;;;;Near clip distance used for tacmap camera wheight height is below tacmap_near_clip_height_threshold:::::tacmap_rotate_speed_multiplier;;;;;how fast tacmap rotates:::::tacmap_smoothing_decay;;;;;determines smoothing applied to tacmap movement:::::tacmap_starts_low;;;;;if true, camera starts at most zoomed in point:::::tacmap_transition_duration_s;;;;;how long camera pan takes in secs:::::tacmap_unit_draw_dist;;;;;Distance tacmap camera is from highest point on map before render units:::::tacmap_zoom_speed_multiplier;;;;;how much scroll changes height when zoom:::::tacmap_zoom_to_cursor;;;;;if true, camera zooms towards cursor, otherwise zooms straight dow",
            },
        },
