        "_kv_winds_of_magic_params_tables": {
            "key": {
                "lookup_hardcoded": "base_multiplier_for_estimated_max_recharge;;;;;(Mainly for UI) For the recharge base, how much extra do we account for to consider max (basically from bonuses etc.):::::campaign_ui_max_depletion_modifier;;;;;Max value used for winds of magic bar when calculating percentage to show bar at. No logical min/max so use this to balance what bar looks like at different modifier values:::::campaign_ui_min_depletion_modifier;;;;;Min value used for winds of magic bar when calculating percentage to show bar at. No logical min/max so use this to balance what bar looks like at different modifier values:::::depletion_factor;;;;;what we square the used mana by to find the restored points curve. Make this above 0.0. Any values Greater than 1.0 means exponential falloff, below 1.0 means sharp inital falloff(inverse exponential). 1.0f means linear falloff.:::::depletion_full_amount;;;;;How much mana should be consider \'full depletion\':::::pool_max_amount;;;;;the absolute max that can be in the mana pool:::::pool_start_max;;;;;the upper range of which the starting mana can be:::::pool_start_min;;;;;the lower range of which the starting mana can be:::::restored_points_base;;;;;how much would we restore per second if everything was \'vanilla\'",
            },
        },
